mber and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper actions. Statistical trends alone do not indicate wrongdoing, as market conditions or budget constraints could explain the data.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and awardees to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the terms of contract [1] to confirm if the amount was near the limit due to market rates or budget constraints.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["0sFbU2K7Z%2FSFQ%2FlhRK79lA%3D%3D","BPLGxD%2FHiF7IGlsa0Wad%2Bw%3D%3D","1YXkLwB6G26cCF8sV%2BqtYA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}